    "kind": "news",
    "check": "sixteen nominations for eighteen seats, no poll (BNL 6 Jan 1926); the two unfilled seats are recorded by the 18-seat contest.",
    "url": "https://irishnewsarchive.com/?a=d&d=BNL19260106.1.10"
  },
  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, polled Friday 15 January 1926; no election took place, the nominations of 5 January filling sixteen of the eighteen seats (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1926, p. 10). 'Dr. H. A. Anderson (returning officer) yesterday received sixteen nominations for eighteen seats on the Coleraine Urban Council, and as a consequence there will be no election.' Two seats were therefore left unfilled. No party label was printed. Returned unopposed."
